            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 56-year-old male, who presented on 06/01/2011 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests demonstrated leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed acute appendicitis. The patient was assessed and prepared for surgical intervention. A laparoscopic appendectomy was successfully performed on 07/01/2011 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, the patient received intravenous fluids, analgesics, and prophylactic antibiotics. Wound care was provided throughout the stay. Vital signs remained stable. The patient recovered well and was discharged on 11/01/2011 with oral analgesia and wound care instructions. Please arrange a follow-up appointment in approximately two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>"
            },
